WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.279
Without Mary Austin, it's hard to say where
Freddie Mercury and by extension, Queen would've

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:05.780
ended up.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.720
Austin was a lover, confidant, and friend
to the legendary rock star, and helped Mercury

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.420
reach the heights of superstardom.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:17.340
British-American actress Lucy Boynton played
Austin on the big screen in Bohemian Rhapsody,

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.780
and she sure looked familiar.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.520
Here are a few roles you may have seen Boynton
in before her big breakthrough.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.980
Even though Bohemian Rhapsody gave Boynton
a chance to show off her dramatic acting chops,

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.770
she's made a name for herself in horror movie
circles.

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:35.090
One of her more recent features, Apostle,
is a bloody period piece that fits squarely

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:36.080
in that category.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.550
Apostle tells the story of a man in 1905 trying
to rescue his kidnapped sister from a dangerous

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.820
religious cult on a remote island.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.550
As supplies on the island run low and the
faithful begin to lose hope, the group's leader,

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:52.530
Prophet Malcolm, begins to take more desperate
and drastic measures.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:56.280
Boynton plays Prophet Malcolm's daughter,
Andrea, who is beginning to understand the

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.020
evil that her father is capable of.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:03.780
Bohemian Rhapsody was not Boynton's first
turn in a star-studded major motion picture.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:08.369
Just a year before the Oscar-nominated biopic,
the actress was cast as Countess Elena in

00:01:08.369 --> 00:01:12.810
director Kenneth Branagh's retelling of the
Agatha Christie classic Murder on the Orient

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:13.660
Express.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:18.460
The timid Countess hides a shadowy past and
continually takes drugs to help her sleep

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.240
during the day.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:24.320
As such, Boynton described the character to
Vanity Fair as being easily confused, because

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.020
she's frequently unsure whether it's day or
night.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:31.560
To help convey that sense, the actress tried
to express, quote, "a feeling of a slightly

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.780
damaged butterfly."

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.020
In an interview with W magazine, Boynton said
that she would like to play a wide variety

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:41.360
of characters in her career, but darker roles
appeals to her more.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.960
That would certainly apply to her role in
the Netflix series Gypsy.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:49.540
Boynton plays Allison Adams, a pill addict
who is seeking treatment from a therapist

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.720
played by Naomi Watts, a woman with her own
set of issues.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:56.760
As Allison gets deeper into her treatment,
Jean struggles to stay within the typical

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.640
boundaries that exist between a counselor
and her patient.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:03.780
Boynton talked with Entertainment Weekly about
the experience of making the show, saying

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:08.009
she was drawn to the dark project because
the writing allows viewers to see, quote,

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:10.140
"the truest, dirtiest sides of people."

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:16.010
Speaking of dark projects, director Polly
Steele's Let Me Go was crowdfunded and based

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:20.940
on the autobiographical book of the same name
by Helga Schneider about learning that her

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.920
estranged mother had been a guard at a Nazi
concentration camp.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.940
The film tells the story from the perspective
of Helga, who, at age 60, receives a letter

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.750
detailing her aging mother's whereabouts.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.990
Along with her daughter Beth and her granddaughter
Emily, played by Boynton, Helga travels to

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:40.690
Vienna to see her mother one last time, where
she finds the matriarch remorseless about

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.200
her role in the Holocaust.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:48.280
Catcher in the Rye author J.D. Salinger was
a notorious recluse until his death in 2010,

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:52.300
and refused to allow a film adaptation of
his novel to be made, saying it was, quote,

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:53.160
"unactable."

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:58.160
Director Danny Strong attempted the next best
thing with Rebel in the Rye, which chronicles

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.480
the life of Salinger as he wrote the landmark
novel.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:05.080
Nicholas Hoult plays a young Salinger, who
along the way meets Claire Douglas, played

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:05.760
by Boynton.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:10.180
In real life, Douglas was the inspiration
for Franny Glass, the character featured in

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.780
Salinger's Franny and Zooey.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.100
Horror films were a hallmark of Lucy Boynton's
early career.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.140
Don't Knock Twice, like Let Me Go, is a story
about mothers and daughters, except with way

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.220
more ghosts.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:27.720
Boynton plays Chloe, a teenager who unwittingly
awakens a witch living in an abandoned house.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:31.480
In an effort to escape the evil, Chloe flees
to the country to stay with her estranged

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.460
mother, Jess.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:37.240
Jess is a successful artist who lives with
her lawyer husband and now wants to reconnect

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:41.150
with her daughter after previously losing
her to foster care because of a substance

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:41.840
abuse problem.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.660
But the witch problem they're all facing now
may prove worse!

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.260
I Am the Pretty Thing That Lives in the House
was the second collaboration between Boynton

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:54.850
and director Osgood "Oz" Perkins, the son
of Psycho star Anthony Perkins.

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:58.600
Much like his father's most famous flick,
the movie centers around a dwelling where

00:03:58.600 --> 00:03:59.920
creepy things happen.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.520
In this case, it's the 200-year-old New England
home of Iris Blum, a popular author of horror

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:06.020
novels.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.620
Things get weird when Miss Blum's new nurse,
Lily, realizes that the old woman is talking

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:14.720
to someone named Polly who doesn't appear
to be there, or is she?

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:19.200
Boyton plays Polly, the main character of
The Lady in the Wall, one of Blum's novels

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.180
from decades ago.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:23.900
But it's possible that Polly is more than
just a fictional character.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:28.040
In flashbacks, Polly is seen as a young woman
condemned to a terrible fate.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.759
Sing Street was Boynton's first lead acting
role, having been previously relegated to

00:04:32.759 --> 00:04:34.060
supporting characters.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:38.009
The musical story about a teenager in Dublin
trying to start a band in order to impress

00:04:38.009 --> 00:04:43.379
a girl was popular at Sundance when it premiered
in 2016, and was nominated for a Golden Globe

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.180
for best picture: musical or comedy.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:46.340
"Why'd you do that, then?"

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.240
"For our art, Cosmo!

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.040
You can never do anything by half."

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:58.000
Boynton plays Raphina, an aspiring model being
wooed by 14-year-old Conor "Cosmo" Lawlor.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:02.380
For Boynton, the film was a new experience
it was one of the few times in her young career

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:04.560
that she was one of the oldest actors on set.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:10.700
In 2015, Boyton teamed up with director Oz
Perkins for the first time in The Blackcoat's

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.289
Daughter, a film that was originally called
February when it made its premiere at the

00:05:14.289 --> 00:05:15.680
Toronto Film Festival.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:19.600
After being held in release date limbo for
more than a year, the movie hit streaming

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.040
services with a new title.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:26.279
In the movie, Kat, played by Kiernan Shipka,
and Rose, played by Boynton, are stuck at

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.000
a Catholic girls' boarding school when a mysterious
young woman arrives.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.760
Before too long, Kat and Rose are left to
battle an unforeseen evil.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:38.740
Copperhead is a period drama that was only
Boynton's second film credit.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:43.960
In the movie, Boynton plays Esther Hagadorn,
daughter of a hardline upstate New York abolitionist

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.060
during the Civil War.

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:48.660
Esther falls in love with Jeff Beech, the
son of a pacifist.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.599
The vast political difference between the
lovers' fathers threatens to derail their

00:05:52.599 --> 00:05:53.599
relationship.

00:05:53.599 --> 00:05:58.020
The movie was based on the book The Copperhead
by Harold Frederic, which examined the differing

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:02.040
political attitudes that existed on the homefront
during America's Civil War.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:06.319
Boynton made her big screen debut in Miss
Potter at the age of 11.

00:06:06.319 --> 00:06:10.419
She was cast as a young Beatrix Potter, the
famed author who created The Tale of Peter

00:06:10.419 --> 00:06:14.800
Rabbit and a number of other classic children's
books with charming animal characters.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:18.110
It didn't take long for young Lucy to be bitten
by the acting bug.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:22.680
She told WWD that on her first day on the
set of Miss Potter, she decided that nothing

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:26.560
else, quote, "could make [her] as happy or
feel as fulfilled as acting does."

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.080
"You can't stand in the way of progress!"

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.200
"So they say."

